      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO three or four times daily**, which is typical for pain or inflammation. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and many clinicians stay at or below 2,400 mg/day.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is common for inflammatory conditions.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg per dose four times daily, please confirm the dose and the indication. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy review would probably be needed. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
